  See also `tf.shape`.

  Returns a 0-D `Tensor` representing the number of elements in `input`
  of type `out_type`. Defaults to tf.int32.

  For example:

  >>> t = tf.constant([[[1, 1, 1], [2, 2, 2]], [[3, 3, 3], [4, 4, 4]]])
